## Model and equations (rendered natively from the recipe)

The model is **generated from the recipe** — the equations and parameters shown are exactly what runs on the backend, not a hand-transcribed copy, so they can be checked one to one against the source they come from. `citeformat="quarto"` makes the render emit the model's own references as inline `@key` citations, resolved by this document's bibliography and merged into the one auto-appended list, which is why the model's citekeys must exist in `references.bib`.

