## Figures

<!-- ONE loop over the recipe's own `figures:` block, never a hand-written list of stems and captions, which drifts from the recipe the moment a figure is added or renamed. Each caption is the figure's own `description:`. `output: asis` prints raw markdown, so the bold lead renders and the description may use LaTeX ($I_0$) — keep it LaTeX and ASCII, never Unicode. -->
```{python}
#| output: asis
for n, fig in enumerate(figures_ordered(STUDY.figures), 1):
    print(f"### {figure_title(fig)}\n")
    staged = report_figure(FIGS / f"{fig.name}.png")
    if staged is None:
        print(f"::: {{.callout-warning}}\n`{fig.name}.png` is not rendered — "
              f"run `tvbo run {study}.yaml`.\n:::\n")
        continue
    print(f"![**Fig {n}.** {figure_caption(fig)}]({embed_path(staged)})"
          f"{{#fig-{fig.name.replace('_', '-')} width=100%}}\n")
```

